{
  "abstract": "Conjecture 213 of DeLaViña's Written on the Wall II (Graffiti.pc) says that a simple connected graph G on n > 1 vertices has a Hamiltonian path if 2 + lm(Ḡ) ≤ γ₂(Ḡ), where Ḡ is the complement of G, lm(Ḡ) the lower median of the degree sequence of Ḡ and γ₂(Ḡ) the 2-domination number of Ḡ. The package proves the conjecture as stated, with no hypothesis beyond the source's. The main theorem reads the lower median as the middle term d_{⌈n/2⌉} of the degree sequence (d_{n/2} for even n, the median d_{(n+1)/2} for odd n). For odd n the catalogue's definition 68 names the term d_{(n+1)/2+1}, which is not the middle term; that literal reading is proved as a variant theorem, which follows from the main one because the literal term is never smaller.",
  "authors": [
